WEBVTT

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:10.930
Onii-chan, is Conny here?

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:13.900
That stupid pig Conny.

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:15.610
What's wrong, Tsukiyo?

00:00:15.610 --> 00:00:16.480
Did Conny...

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:18.370
Look at this, Onii-chan.

00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:21.620
Conny ate my cake again.

00:00:23.530 --> 00:00:25.830
And Sora-san made this for me.

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:29.210
The one you brought home yesterday.

00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:30.750
<i>Oh, that.</i>

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:33.510
This is Tsukiyo-chan's share.

00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:37.100
I was looking forward to 
having it after school.

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:39.760
Sora-san's cakes are special.

00:00:41.990 --> 00:00:45.420
<i>She's always really liked Kashiwagi.</i>

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:52.960
Don't cry. I'll ask him to make more.

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:55.240
I can forgive it once or twice...

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:57.560
But this is the ninth time.

00:00:57.560 --> 00:00:58.530
Ninth?!

00:01:06.220 --> 00:01:07.410
Listen, Conny.

00:01:07.730 --> 00:01:10.840
I've told you plenty of times 
not to eat Tsukiyo's food.

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:14.400
Why don't you listen to me?

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:16.480
You understand me, don't you?

00:01:17.730 --> 00:01:21.840
Hey, don't think you can 
get away with anything.

00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:25.610
I don't need to take care of 
someone who doesn't listen to me.

00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:28.440
When in Rome, do as the Romans do.

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:32.990
If you can't do that, leave. Now.

00:01:44.890 --> 00:01:46.960
I'm not your parent.

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:50.340
My family isn't your family.

00:01:51.070 --> 00:01:53.530
I can't allow this kind of trouble 
to continue happening.

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:23.080
Conny?

00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:03.340
#09
Kind Hands, Warm Hands

00:04:05.090 --> 00:04:07.850
Mukumuku gave me this yesterday.

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:07.850
It's all good

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:09.770
What's all good?

00:04:09.770 --> 00:04:10.780
Dunno.

00:04:10.780 --> 00:04:14.450
It looks like everyone's 
having fun writing letters.

00:04:15.110 --> 00:04:17.860
Mii-kun's been hooked on writing letters.

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:19.940
Always
apples

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:20.860
Always

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:20.860
Together

00:04:19.020 --> 00:04:20.860
Always
apples

00:04:21.770 --> 00:04:25.490
Isn't it a little scary when he keeps 
writing "always together" like that?

00:04:25.490 --> 00:04:30.650
I think he hasn't learned anything besides
"together," "always," "all the time," and "apples."

00:04:30.650 --> 00:04:35.150
I'd thought he'd learned 
letters like Isao had.

00:04:35.150 --> 00:04:36.390
He hasn't?

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:40.580
I think he just memorized them like 
you would symbols or pictures.

00:04:40.950 --> 00:04:42.530
So even when...

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:47.530
Mii-kun explained to Isao 
what he wanted to write,

00:04:47.530 --> 00:04:51.230
and Isao turned it into 
letters so he could write it.

00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:55.060
Isao's a bit too smart.

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:56.420
He's amazing.

00:04:56.420 --> 00:04:59.520
Imagine if he starts writing 
equations and stuff.

00:05:01.050 --> 00:05:02.720
What's wrong, Tacchan?

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:04.650
Nothing.

00:05:04.840 --> 00:05:08.920
Oh, yeah, you didn't bring 
Conny to the shrine today.

00:05:08.920 --> 00:05:10.310
Is something up with Conny?

00:05:11.340 --> 00:05:13.410
It seems like he's gone off somewhere.

00:05:14.370 --> 00:05:16.420
He does what he wants.

00:05:18.940 --> 00:05:20.790
I'm home, Onii-chan.

00:05:21.150 --> 00:05:23.960
Are you making dinner for tonight?

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:24.700
Yeah.

00:05:27.330 --> 00:05:28.800
This is for Conny.

00:05:29.380 --> 00:05:32.010
I said too much yesterday.

00:05:32.460 --> 00:05:33.310
Yeah?

00:05:33.710 --> 00:05:36.060
But he hasn't come downstairs yet.

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:38.330
Normally, he'd come to nag me.

00:05:39.810 --> 00:05:42.920
<i>He never waits this long to eat.</i>

00:05:43.820 --> 00:05:45.550
<i>He's still not home?</i>

00:05:47.590 --> 00:05:49.560
Hey, Conny, stop hiding.

00:05:49.560 --> 00:05:50.700
Come out if you're here.

00:05:58.610 --> 00:06:03.210
Damn it, what is he out doing this late?

00:06:03.740 --> 00:06:05.710
Leave. Now.

00:06:07.380 --> 00:06:11.010
<i>Could he have actually left?</i>

00:06:12.430 --> 00:06:15.100
<i>I've been trying to kick him 
out since the beginning.</i>

00:06:15.750 --> 00:06:20.930
<i>I'd never even told him 
to stay or to come home.</i>

00:06:26.930 --> 00:06:30.490
<i>What kind of face am I supposed 
to put on, looking for him now?</i>

00:06:36.890 --> 00:06:39.070
Tazuki, is something wrong?

00:06:40.060 --> 00:06:41.140
Your bangs.

00:06:42.340 --> 00:06:45.280
That's what happens to your hair 
when you don't get enough sleep.

00:06:45.280 --> 00:06:47.190
You didn't sleep well last night, did you?

00:06:47.820 --> 00:06:48.840
I'm fine.

00:06:49.250 --> 00:06:51.300
My eyes just aren't working right today.

00:06:51.770 --> 00:06:53.500
Are you really okay?

00:06:53.500 --> 00:06:54.510
Yeah.

00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:57.020
<b>Delicious
Red Bean Soup</b>

00:06:55.920 --> 00:06:57.880
<i>Yeah, right.</i>

00:06:58.780 --> 00:07:00.020
I made a mistake.

00:07:05.010 --> 00:07:06.030
Kamiya-kun.

00:07:06.780 --> 00:07:09.500
Kamiya-kun, your textbook is upside down.

00:07:12.170 --> 00:07:14.370
<i>He's totally not okay.</i>

00:07:24.110 --> 00:07:26.170
Conny never came home?!

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:27.100
Yeah.

00:07:27.100 --> 00:07:28.300
You didn't go look for him?

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:29.930
Of course not.

00:07:29.930 --> 00:07:30.990
It was the middle of the night.

00:07:32.240 --> 00:07:33.250
Oh, right.

00:07:33.990 --> 00:07:35.720
Then let's all go look for 
him together after school.

00:07:35.720 --> 00:07:37.260
We don't need to do that.

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:40.260
He left of his own volition.

00:07:40.670 --> 00:07:42.110
We don't need to look for him.

00:07:42.110 --> 00:07:45.920
Maybe he's just lost.

00:07:45.920 --> 00:07:47.320
That's fine, too.

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:49.570
It's not my problem.

00:07:52.610 --> 00:07:54.220
Tazuki, why are you...

00:07:54.220 --> 00:07:55.190
Stop.

00:07:55.190 --> 00:07:56.590
Don't make me repeat myself.

00:07:59.740 --> 00:08:01.080
<i>He says that,</i>

00:08:01.870 --> 00:08:04.440
<i>but it's written all over
his face that he's worried.</i>

00:08:26.090 --> 00:08:28.610
Hey, Tacchan, do you have club work now?

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:29.730
Yeah.

00:08:29.730 --> 00:08:32.050
But I heard Conny's missing.

00:08:32.050 --> 00:08:33.690
Just leave him be.

00:08:35.420 --> 00:08:37.930
Hey, Tazuki, about that...

00:08:37.930 --> 00:08:40.010
Can I go look for him?

00:08:40.010 --> 00:08:41.090
Me, too.

00:08:41.090 --> 00:08:42.230
I'll go, too.

00:08:42.230 --> 00:08:45.710
Dude, Conny's missing? Really?

00:08:45.990 --> 00:08:47.680
We need to go look for him.

00:08:47.680 --> 00:08:48.870
Yeah.

00:08:48.870 --> 00:08:50.990
I can't have you looking for him.

00:08:51.950 --> 00:08:54.590
I told you to leave him be. 
Don't you understand?

00:08:56.280 --> 00:08:57.490
Are you sure?

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:05.100
Why would I say so if I wasn't?

00:09:10.550 --> 00:09:15.010
<i>He tends to let things 
fester when they happen.</i>

00:09:15.580 --> 00:09:19.870
<i>He didn't seem to want anyone asking, 
so I pretended not to notice...</i>

00:09:20.210 --> 00:09:23.330
<i>But I don't think that'll cut it this time.</i>

00:09:27.160 --> 00:09:30.630
<i>Are those guys seriously 
going to look for him?</i>

00:09:50.910 --> 00:09:52.520
Found you.

00:09:55.280 --> 00:09:57.450
Hey, don't slam the door like that.

00:09:57.450 --> 00:09:59.200
What if you were to break it?

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:00.430
My bad.

00:10:03.160 --> 00:10:06.880
Kamiya, what's up? Let's go to club.

00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:10.410
Kamiya?

00:10:11.290 --> 00:10:13.630
Sorry, I'm taking the day off.

00:10:14.470 --> 00:10:15.780
Kamiya!

00:10:24.070 --> 00:10:25.890
<i>I have to stop them.</i>

00:10:26.320 --> 00:10:28.630
<i>They've got to be kidding about 
actually looking for him.</i>

00:10:29.830 --> 00:10:31.900
Mii-kun, has Conny been here?

00:10:34.280 --> 00:10:36.150
So he's not at the shrine, either?

00:10:37.300 --> 00:10:40.770
Conny hasn't been home since yesterday.

00:10:41.750 --> 00:10:43.830
Where else could he be?

00:10:44.560 --> 00:10:46.810
Let's split up and look for him.

00:10:46.810 --> 00:10:47.540
Yeah.

00:10:50.150 --> 00:10:51.280
Mii-kun.

00:10:52.540 --> 00:10:54.420
You have to stay here.

00:10:54.640 --> 00:10:57.550
Isao, take good care of Mii-kun.

00:10:57.550 --> 00:10:58.670
You, too, Mukumuku.

00:11:00.960 --> 00:11:02.860
It's all right, Mii-kun.

00:11:04.190 --> 00:11:06.170
We'll be back by nightfall.

00:11:06.170 --> 00:11:08.060
And we'll bring Conny.

00:11:08.900 --> 00:11:11.440
Don't cry and hang on, Mii-kun.

00:11:19.030 --> 00:11:20.690
<i>That meddler...</i>

00:11:22.180 --> 00:11:25.750
<i>You, Mii,</i>

00:11:26.390 --> 00:11:28.140
<i>Isao and Mogi,</i>

00:11:28.950 --> 00:11:30.990
<i>Mukumuku and Tachiaki,</i>

00:11:32.120 --> 00:11:34.050
<i>you and Mokuren...</i>

00:11:36.130 --> 00:11:38.180
<i>I'm seriously getting worried about you.</i>

00:11:38.180 --> 00:11:40.460
<i>I don't want more things to worry about.</i>

00:11:41.880 --> 00:11:43.740
<i>Where might they have gone?</i>

00:11:47.290 --> 00:11:51.350
<i>I can't help but have dreams 
about that day when he's at home.</i>

00:11:52.440 --> 00:11:57.110
<i>Yet, there was no way I 
could actually kick him out.</i>

00:11:58.140 --> 00:12:02.100
<i>So I was a tiny bit relieved when he left.</i>

00:12:03.070 --> 00:12:07.370
<i>He's selfish, violent and 
doesn't listen to me.</i>

00:12:07.700 --> 00:12:09.370
<i>He makes a mess in the bath.</i>

00:12:09.370 --> 00:12:11.370
<i>He sneaks into my bed.</i>

00:12:14.620 --> 00:12:16.230
<i>He's a pain.</i>

00:12:16.230 --> 00:12:17.670
<i>Annoying.</i>

00:12:17.670 --> 00:12:18.870
<i>I want to kick him out.</i>

00:12:19.400 --> 00:12:20.330
<i>So why...</i>

00:12:20.930 --> 00:12:21.910
<i>So why...</i>

00:12:23.970 --> 00:12:30.330
<i>Why am I so desperate to find that child oni?</i>

00:12:31.700 --> 00:12:32.860
Tazuki.

00:12:33.390 --> 00:12:34.730
Why are you here?

00:12:35.730 --> 00:12:36.770
What about your club?

00:12:37.130 --> 00:12:38.290
I took the day off.

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:42.400
Conny!

00:12:44.090 --> 00:12:45.110
Wait.

00:12:49.180 --> 00:12:50.320
<i>He's up there!</i>

00:12:50.320 --> 00:12:51.370
Conny!

00:12:52.010 --> 00:12:52.870
<i>Damn it!</i>

00:12:52.870 --> 00:12:54.870
Hey, listen to me!

00:12:56.580 --> 00:12:58.740
He doesn't want to listen to me, does he?

00:12:58.740 --> 00:13:01.190
<i>I may have said too much.</i>

00:13:01.880 --> 00:13:03.930
<i>And I think I said it in an awful way.</i>

00:13:04.470 --> 00:13:05.760
But still...

00:13:07.180 --> 00:13:08.260
<i>Still...</i>

00:13:10.570 --> 00:13:15.640
Still, I would never 
actually tell you to leave!

00:13:18.180 --> 00:13:19.090
Which way?

00:13:19.520 --> 00:13:21.280
Find which way he went.

00:13:25.480 --> 00:13:26.930
Right, Kashiwagi.

00:13:27.240 --> 00:13:28.590
He's going up the hill.

00:13:29.140 --> 00:13:30.370
<i>This is stupid.</i>

00:13:30.970 --> 00:13:34.000
<i>My body is way more honest than my head.</i>

00:13:34.370 --> 00:13:38.430
<i>He wasn't the reason I get anxious or scared.</i>

00:13:39.390 --> 00:13:42.800
<i>My emotions got all mixed
up and I said awful things to him.</i>

00:13:43.440 --> 00:13:45.710
<i>This is pathetic. Man up!</i>

00:13:46.200 --> 00:13:48.620
<i>I should have confronted him earlier.</i>

00:13:49.510 --> 00:13:52.250
<i>Him, </i>and<i> myself.</i>

00:13:57.520 --> 00:14:00.520
For sale

00:13:59.220 --> 00:14:00.520
What?

00:14:01.010 --> 00:14:03.530
Wait, Conny, talk to me.

00:14:04.150 --> 00:14:05.120
Please.

00:14:05.120 --> 00:14:06.860
Just stop for a second.

00:14:12.190 --> 00:14:14.160
It's not Conny!

00:14:42.220 --> 00:14:43.570
Really?

00:14:45.920 --> 00:14:46.760
Conny?

00:14:50.480 --> 00:14:51.390
Is that you?

00:14:52.800 --> 00:14:53.900
You're stuck?

00:14:54.830 --> 00:14:55.830
What the hell?

00:14:56.780 --> 00:14:58.520
I can't believe it.

00:14:58.520 --> 00:14:59.830
You're kidding me.

00:15:00.700 --> 00:15:02.600
I'll help you out, so stop squirming.

00:15:02.900 --> 00:15:04.560
You're just going to get 
yourself even more stuck.

00:15:06.180 --> 00:15:09.340
What were you doing in this hole to begin with?

00:15:09.880 --> 00:15:12.440
Come on, suck your gut in.

00:15:16.370 --> 00:15:17.830
You idiot!

00:15:17.830 --> 00:15:19.640
What if I hadn't noticed you?

00:15:22.490 --> 00:15:26.110
No, I was an idiot, too.

00:15:30.270 --> 00:15:31.590
Let's talk later.

00:15:32.410 --> 00:15:34.400
There's a lot I want to talk to you about.

00:15:34.790 --> 00:15:38.750
Tazuki, sorry, it wasn't Conny.

00:15:38.970 --> 00:15:40.210
It was the wrong oni.

00:15:40.210 --> 00:15:42.230
But we'll find Conny, I swear.

00:15:42.230 --> 00:15:44.690
I'll share half of your burden.

00:15:44.690 --> 00:15:45.670
So...

00:15:45.670 --> 00:15:46.650
Tacchan!

00:15:48.740 --> 00:15:50.380
What do we do, you guys?

00:15:50.760 --> 00:15:52.810
We found his pants floating in the river.

00:15:52.810 --> 00:15:53.760
These.

00:15:53.760 --> 00:15:57.750
We looked all around, but we couldn't 
find the child oni they belong to.

00:15:57.750 --> 00:16:00.520
D-D-Do you think it's Conny?

00:16:00.520 --> 00:16:01.440
Which river?

00:16:01.440 --> 00:16:02.270
Let's go look.

00:16:02.270 --> 00:16:03.400
Stop, stop, stop.

00:16:03.680 --> 00:16:05.030
I found Conny.

00:16:10.900 --> 00:16:13.250
Conny!

00:16:13.910 --> 00:16:15.480
Thank goodness!

00:16:15.480 --> 00:16:18.350
So they <i>are</i> your pants!

00:16:19.160 --> 00:16:21.630
Wait, you guys are both wet.

00:16:21.630 --> 00:16:23.670
It must be because we jumped in the river.

00:16:23.670 --> 00:16:24.720
Seriously?

00:16:28.100 --> 00:16:29.170
Thanks.

00:16:30.680 --> 00:16:33.140
Sorry to make you guys worry.

00:16:33.650 --> 00:16:34.620
Thanks.

00:16:36.550 --> 00:16:37.500
Yeah.

00:16:37.500 --> 00:16:39.280
Come on, don't be so formal.

00:16:39.280 --> 00:16:41.000
Yeah!

00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:43.810
You need to depend on your friends more.

00:16:44.100 --> 00:16:46.410
Before you start getting your 
tea and red bean soup mixed up.

00:16:46.840 --> 00:16:49.200
Before you start reading 
your textbook upside down.

00:16:49.810 --> 00:16:51.690
Damn it, you guys.

00:16:54.340 --> 00:16:58.400
Mii-kun, Isao, Mukumuku, we found Con—

00:17:03.110 --> 00:17:04.110
Wow.

00:17:04.110 --> 00:17:05.200
Seriously?

00:17:06.540 --> 00:17:11.460
Welcome Home

00:17:13.970 --> 00:17:15.930
Everyone was worried about you.

00:17:18.140 --> 00:17:21.600
Mii, Isao, Mukumuku,

00:17:22.060 --> 00:17:26.350
Kashiwagi, Mogi, Tachiaki, Tsukiyo,

00:17:26.870 --> 00:17:27.950
and also...

00:17:30.310 --> 00:17:31.690
me.

00:17:31.690 --> 00:17:32.760
I think.

00:17:32.760 --> 00:17:34.040
Kind of.

00:17:38.110 --> 00:17:39.950
Later. See you tomorrow.

00:17:40.680 --> 00:17:43.260
I'll walk Mogi-chan home part way.

00:17:43.260 --> 00:17:44.160
Yeah.

00:17:44.160 --> 00:17:45.250
Thanks.

00:17:45.660 --> 00:17:47.250
Be honest.

00:17:47.460 --> 00:17:49.710
Yeah, I know.

00:17:53.390 --> 00:17:55.070
Let's talk on our way home.

00:17:56.460 --> 00:17:58.340
It'll be easier that way.

00:17:59.700 --> 00:18:02.560
There are two things I want to tell you.

00:18:03.400 --> 00:18:05.780
First, about the day before yesterday.

00:18:06.480 --> 00:18:09.290
I'm sorry I told you to leave.

00:18:10.150 --> 00:18:11.970
I shouldn't have said you aren't family.

00:18:12.790 --> 00:18:15.780
Still, what you did was wrong.

00:18:18.280 --> 00:18:23.800
For example, wouldn't you be sad 
if someone else ate your snack?

00:18:24.880 --> 00:18:28.480
I want you to think about how Tsukiyo felt.

00:18:30.870 --> 00:18:33.510
Second, about you and me...

00:18:34.870 --> 00:18:38.880
A long time ago, I found a dragon that 
was being chased down by a collector.

00:18:39.940 --> 00:18:44.300
I was going to save him, but I 
ended up putting it in danger.

00:18:46.080 --> 00:18:48.530
I heard it's doing well now,

00:18:49.720 --> 00:18:53.580
but with what had happened, I didn't 
feel like I could protect you.

00:18:54.670 --> 00:18:57.740
That's why I rejected you.

00:18:59.080 --> 00:19:04.450
That doesn't mean I don't want 
you around, or that I hate you.

00:19:07.080 --> 00:19:10.850
What I'm saying is that you were annoying 
at first, but you've gotten better.

00:19:10.850 --> 00:19:12.210
Don't get the wrong idea.

00:19:13.450 --> 00:19:14.690
No, sorry.

00:19:14.690 --> 00:19:15.770
I mean...

00:19:16.710 --> 00:19:19.390
I don't like saying this 
kind of thing out loud.

00:19:19.860 --> 00:19:20.840
I didn't mean that.

00:19:21.740 --> 00:19:25.160
I'm not good at taking care 
of people like Kashiwagi is,

00:19:25.160 --> 00:19:27.790
nor can I pamper you like Mogi does.

00:19:28.700 --> 00:19:30.110
This is the best I can do.

00:19:32.800 --> 00:19:35.110
If that's good enough, stay with me.

00:19:36.520 --> 00:19:38.960
If you get lost, I'll look 
for you until I find you.

00:19:38.960 --> 00:19:40.860
If something happens, I'll come get you.

00:19:41.450 --> 00:19:42.910
So come home.

00:19:43.660 --> 00:19:45.370
Let's have you live at my place properly.

00:19:57.150 --> 00:20:00.440
Come on, Mommy, let's go home already.

00:20:24.840 --> 00:20:27.030
Wait, you cry?

00:20:27.030 --> 00:20:28.470
I've never seen you cry.

00:20:30.400 --> 00:20:32.920
So, what do you think?

00:20:36.520 --> 00:20:37.510
All right.

00:20:38.520 --> 00:20:39.490
Good.

00:20:52.190 --> 00:20:56.670
Oh, that hydrangea was 
a gift to Tsukiyo-chan?

00:20:56.670 --> 00:20:57.740
Yeah.

00:20:57.740 --> 00:21:01.530
Apparently he felt bad about 
having eaten the cake.

00:21:04.350 --> 00:21:07.350
He stopped eating other people's food now,

00:21:07.350 --> 00:21:11.070
and he's starting to listen to what I say.

00:21:11.560 --> 00:21:14.340
He wouldn't listen to me before.

00:21:14.840 --> 00:21:18.300
Maybe that's because you accepted him.

00:21:19.270 --> 00:21:23.550
Conny was like a kid who caused trouble 
trying to draw his parents' attention.

00:21:24.480 --> 00:21:28.140
Maybe he wanted you to say he can stay.

00:21:28.980 --> 00:21:31.430
That's a pain, too.

00:21:31.640 --> 00:21:34.840
Jeez, you're never honest, Tacchan.

00:21:34.840 --> 00:21:37.480
You were back then, though.

00:21:38.440 --> 00:21:43.190
Still, I would never 
actually tell you to leave.

00:21:43.740 --> 00:21:46.810
Although you weren't shouting at Conny.

00:21:48.110 --> 00:21:50.710
You should just be more honest with yourself.

00:21:50.710 --> 00:21:54.220
You say he's a pain, and that he isn't cute,

00:21:54.220 --> 00:21:57.620
but you end up showing 
it on your face anyway.

00:22:00.500 --> 00:22:02.970
Kami-kun's pretty easy to read, huh?

00:22:02.970 --> 00:22:03.770
Shut up.

00:22:03.770 --> 00:22:04.940
Let me be.

00:22:04.940 --> 00:22:06.950
This is just right for me.

00:22:10.140 --> 00:22:14.180
What do you think?

00:22:13.140 --> 00:22:19.900
What do you think?

00:22:17.560 --> 00:22:19.140
Right back at you.

00:23:51.430 --> 00:23:55.220
Mii-kun was flailing his arms 
and legs during his nap.

00:23:55.220 --> 00:23:57.380
I wonder if mummies have dreams, too.

00:23:57.380 --> 00:23:59.810
I hope it was a fun dream.

00:23:59.790 --> 00:24:04.710
Next Episode
A Fun Surprise from Afar

00:24:00.620 --> 00:24:01.910
How to Keep a Mummy.

00:24:01.910 --> 00:24:03.500
See you next episode.

00:24:04.710 --> 00:24:08.000
<b>See you next time!</b>
